# JS / AJAX APP Namespace Standard

- Use `$.ajax()` only — never `fetch()` or raw XHR.
- Every AJAX call: `beforeSend` (disable btn) + `complete` (re-enable) + `error` callback — mandatory.
- Use `APP.csrf()` for CSRF token — never hardcode.
- Feedback: `APP.toast(msg, 'success|error|warning')` — never `alert()` or inline Bootstrap alert clones.
- Global 401 handling already in base layout via `$.ajaxSetup` — do not re-implement per page.
- Page JS → `<?= $this->section('scripts') ?>` block. Reusable JS → `public/assets/js/`.
- Never redeclare `APP.*` functions per page — call or extend existing helpers.
- Check `response.status === 'success'` (not HTTP code) for app-level success.
